# Components, API, SEO, Security

## Components

- Server Components by default. `"use client"` only for interactivity, hooks, or browser APIs.
- Keep components small and reusable. Avoid unnecessary re-renders and client boundaries.

## Images

- Use `next/image`. Prefer WebP/AVIF, compress, lazy-load (except LCP/hero when needed).
- Never serve oversized assets.

## API

- Validate input; return only required fields; keep payloads small.
- Handle errors properly; protect admin/authenticated routes.
- Avoid unnecessary client → API hops when the server can load data directly.

## SEO

- Correct `metadata` / Open Graph. Keep sitemap and robots.txt accurate.

## Security & logging

- Never expose secrets; use env vars. Sanitize/validate all inputs.
- No noisy `console.log` in production paths; log meaningful errors only.

## Packages & deploy

- Do not add packages without need; prefer Next.js built-ins.
- Stay compatible with AWS Lightsail + Ubuntu + PM2 + Nginx + GitHub Actions.
